chel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ricky Muir","party":"Australian Motoring Enthusiast Party","person_id":"tvfy_10834","person_slug":"ricky-muir","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Robert Simms","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10842","person_slug":"robert-simms","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sam Dastyari","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10819","person_slug":"sam-dastyari","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Conroy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10142","person_slug":"stephen-conroy","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions - Election of Senators - Refer to Committee","noes":38,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2016-02-24.160.1), which means that it was unsuccessful. Senator [Anne McEwen](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/sa/anne_mcewen) (SA, Australian Labor Party), along with several minor-party senators - [Muir](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/victoria/ricky_muir), [Leyonhjelm](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/david_leyonhjelm), [Lazarus](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/queensland/glenn_lazarus), [Madigan](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/victoria/john_madigan), [Wang](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/wa/dio_wang), [Day](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/sa/bob_day) and [Lambie](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/tasmania/jacqui_lambie) - proposed a motion: > That the provisions of the [Commonwealth Electoral Amendment Bill 2016](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation/billhome/r5626) be referred to the [Joint Standing Committee on Electoral Matters](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Committees/Joint/Electoral_Matters) for inquiry and report by 12 May 2016. The Commonwealth Electoral Amendment Bill 2016 is the bill concerning the widely-discussed changes to the way Senate elections work. Given that the report was scheduled to be tabled on 2 March, this motion was to delay discussion of the Bill for roughly 2 months.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4095","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2016-02-24/1"}
